# Claude Installation & Setup Guide (English)

[한국어 가이드](./claude.ko.md) · [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/releases/latest)

## Before You Start

1. In Claire Bible **Account Settings** (`/settings/account`), switch **Extraction mode** to **`Agent Client (client)`**.
2. Keep **MCP Settings** (`/settings/mcp`) open so you can copy your `/mcp` endpoint URL.

## Install & Connect via GUI

1. Open **Marketplace management** in Claude.
2. Enter **`{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}`** (or `https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}.git`), sync, and install **`claire`**.
3. In Claude Connectors / MCP settings, add your remote HTTP server as **`claire`** pointing to `https://<your-claire-server>/mcp`.
4. Complete the browser OAuth 2.1 flow and approve both `readonly` and `write` scopes.

## Slash Commands Ready to Use

- **`/claire:ingest <url, file, or note>`**: Stage a URL, local document file (PDF, DOCX, ODT, MD, TXT), or note and run isolated extraction via `extractor` in one step.
- **`/claire:extract`**: Claim and extract queued `pending` sources waiting in your personal KB.
- **`/claire:query <question>`**: Discover KBs via `kb_list`, search entities and relations, inspect documents, or submit contributions.

<details>
<summary>CLI / Terminal setup</summary>

```text
/plugin marketplace add {{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}
```

Install `claire`, then register the standalone `claire` MCP server:

```bash
claude mcp add --transport http claire https://<your-claire-server>/mcp
```

</details>
